    <h1>EmailToPDFA Jar How-To</h1>
    <p>This message describes how to run the packaged jar and generate EA-PDF output.</p>

    <h2>Artifact</h2>
    <p><code>emailtopdfa.jar</code></p>

    <h2>Requirements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Java 21</li>
      <li>Bundled defaults are included for the font, ICC profile, and ThinkBox logo</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Basic Command</h2>
    <pre>java -jar emailtopdfa.jar message.eml</pre>

    <h2>Accepted Inputs</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>.eml</code></li>
      <li><code>.msg</code></li>
      <li><code>.pst</code></li>
      <li>A directory containing those files</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Single-Message Output</h2>
    <pre>java -jar emailtopdfa.jar message.msg</pre>

    <h2>Single-Message Isolated Output (1si)</h2>
    <pre>java -jar emailtopdfa.jar --omit-source message.eml</pre>

    <h2>Multi-Message Archive Output</h2>
    <p><strong>1m</strong></p>
    <pre>java -jar emailtopdfa.jar --archive-profile m --archive-output archive_1m.pdf archive.pst</pre>

    <p><strong>1mi</strong></p>
    <pre>java -jar emailtopdfa.jar --archive-profile mi --archive-output archive_1mi.pdf archive.pst</pre>

    <h2>Optional Arguments</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>--global-id &lt;id&gt;</code></li>
      <li><code>--email &lt;address&gt;</code> (repeatable)</li>
      <li><code>--jobs &lt;n&gt;</code></li>
      <li><code>--debug</code></li>
      <li><code>--debug-dir &lt;dir&gt;</code></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Gmail Downloader</h2>
    <pre>java -cp emailtopdfa.jar eapdf.GmailDownloadToPdf</pre>

    <h2>Archive Gmail Output</h2>
    <pre>java -cp emailtopdfa.jar eapdf.GmailDownloadToPdf --archive-profile mi --archive-output gmail_archive_1mi.pdf</pre>

    <h2>Notes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>java -jar emailtopdfa.jar</code> runs <code>eapdf.EmailToPDFA</code>.</li>
      <li>Use <code>java -cp emailtopdfa.jar eapdf.GmailDownloadToPdf ...</code> for Gmail mode.</li>
      <li>Single-message output defaults to <code>out</code> if you do not pass <code>--out</code>.</li>
      <li>Archive output defaults to <code>out</code> if you do not pass <code>--archive-output</code>.</li>
    </ul>
  </body>
